option.PT_GI=Diffuse Global Illumination
option.PT_GI.comment=Enables diffuse continuation after direct lighting. Direct diffuse light remains when disabled.
value.PT_GI.0=Off
value.PT_GI.1=On
option.PT_GI_STRENGTH=Diffuse Bounce Gain
option.PT_GI_STRENGTH.comment=Gain applied at each diffuse continuation. 1.0 is energy based; other values are artistic.
option.PT_REFLECTIONS=Reflections
option.PT_REFLECTIONS.comment=Enables the reflective BSDF lobe on opaque surfaces, glass and water. Metals become dark when disabled.
value.PT_REFLECTIONS.0=Off
value.PT_REFLECTIONS.1=On
option.PT_REFLECTION_STRENGTH=Reflection Gain
option.PT_REFRACTION=Refraction
option.PT_REFRACTION.comment=Bends transmitted paths with Snell law. Off transmits straight while retaining material tint.
value.PT_REFRACTION.0=Off
value.PT_REFRACTION.1=On
option.PT_GLASS=Glass Optics
option.PT_GLASS.comment=Enables glass Fresnel, refraction and absorption. Off makes glass interfaces optically neutral.
value.PT_GLASS.0=Off
value.PT_GLASS.1=On
option.PT_CAUSTICS=Caustic Paths
option.PT_CAUSTICS.comment=Allows specular dielectric paths after an opaque bounce. Primary views through glass and water remain.
value.PT_CAUSTICS.0=Off
value.PT_CAUSTICS.1=On
option.PT_CAUSTICS_STRENGTH=Caustic Gain
option.PT_CAUSTICS_STRENGTH.comment=Gain for paths crossing a dielectric after an opaque event. 1.0 preserves transport energy.
option.PT_SHADOWS=Direct Light Shadows
option.PT_SHADOWS.comment=Tests direct-light connections against actual terrain. Off is an artistic unoccluded-light preview.
value.PT_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.PT_SHADOWS.1=On
option.PT_SUNLIGHT=Sun and Moon Light
option.PT_SUNLIGHT.comment=Samples the sun or moon as a finite disc separately from the environment.
value.PT_SUNLIGHT.0=Off
value.PT_SUNLIGHT.1=On
option.PT_SKYLIGHT=Environment Light
option.PT_SKYLIGHT.comment=Enables the sky environment as emitted radiance, tested against scene geometry.
value.PT_SKYLIGHT.0=Off
value.PT_SKYLIGHT.1=On
option.PT_SKY_STRENGTH=Environment Gain
option.PT_LIGHT_SAMPLES=Emitter Samples
option.PT_LIGHT_SAMPLES.comment=Shadow-tested area-emitter estimates at each scattering event. Each estimate resamples Emitter Candidates; higher values trace more visibility rays.
option.PT_RESOLUTION=PT Render Scale
option.PT_RESOLUTION.comment=Internal transport resolution per axis. Lower values trace fewer pixels and save history memory; fine reflected/transmitted detail may be lost. Full-resolution material textures and the HUD stay unchanged. Not AMD FSR or frame generation.
option.PT_FILTER_STRENGTH=Diffuse Filter Strength
option.PT_FILTER_STRENGTH.comment=Spatial reconstruction of diffuse lighting only. Higher values reduce noise but soften illumination boundaries. Surface textures remain full resolution.
option.PT_SPECULAR_FILTER=Specular Filter Strength
option.PT_SPECULAR_FILTER.comment=Compact filtering for reflections, transmission and volume transport. Lower values retain reflected detail but reveal more Monte Carlo noise.
option.PT_SAMPLES=Paths Per Pixel
option.PT_SAMPLES.comment=Independent paths per lighting pixel and frame. More samples reduce noise at a direct GPU cost.
option.PT_BOUNCES=Scattering Events
option.PT_BOUNCES.comment=Maximum opaque-surface or volume-scattering events. Water/glass interfaces use their separate Interface Limit.
option.PT_DISTANCE=Ray Length
option.PT_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum segment length. Increasing this does not increase Scene Capture Range or load chunks.
option.PT_HISTORY=History Frames
option.PT_HISTORY.comment=Maximum accumulated frames. More frames reduce stationary noise; motion and geometry changes reject history.
option.PT_OUTLIER_FILTER=Isolated Sparkle Filter
option.PT_OUTLIER_FILTER.comment=Suppresses isolated bright samples on compatible opaque surfaces. Biased reconstruction; mirrors and glass are exempt.
value.PT_OUTLIER_FILTER.0=Off
value.PT_OUTLIER_FILTER.1=On
option.PT_DENOISE=Spatial Reconstruction
option.PT_DENOISE.comment=Filters diffuse irradiance and specular transport separately using geometry and estimated variance. Full-resolution diffuse textures and visible emission stay outside the filter.
value.PT_DENOISE.0=Off
value.PT_DENOISE.1=On
option.PT_TEMPORAL=Temporal Accumulation
option.PT_TEMPORAL.comment=Accumulates successive camera paths. Moving reflections, moving lights or block edits can retain short-lived history.
value.PT_TEMPORAL.0=Off
value.PT_TEMPORAL.1=On
option.PT_CAUSTIC_GUIDING=Underwater Caustic Sampling
option.PT_CAUSTIC_GUIDING.comment=Samples extra directions toward refracted sunlight underwater, using matching PDFs. Does not project an artificial caustic texture.
value.PT_CAUSTIC_GUIDING.0=Off
value.PT_CAUSTIC_GUIDING.1=On
option.PT_VOLUMETRICS=Path Traced Scattering
option.PT_VOLUMETRICS.comment=Clouds also require this switch. Enables stochastic scattering in air and water. Absorption remains controlled by optical density.
value.PT_VOLUMETRICS.0=Off
value.PT_VOLUMETRICS.1=On
option.PT_AIR_DENSITY=Air Scattering Density
option.PT_AIR_DENSITY.comment=Homogeneous air scattering coefficient. Zero removes air extinction. Water uses its own absorption and scattering controls.
option.PT_GLASS_IOR=Glass Refractive Index
option.PT_GLASS_IOR.comment=Refractive index for captured glass boundaries. Water has its own refractive index under Water.
option.PT_SUN_ANGLE=Sun Angular Radius (Radians)
option.PT_SUN_ANGLE.comment=Finite sun/moon disc radius. A wider disc changes physical shadow softness and caustics while preserving integrated light power.
option.PT_FIREFLY_CLAMP=Radiance Clamp
option.PT_FIREFLY_CLAMP.comment=0 leaves transport unclamped. Positive values bias high-energy paths to reduce rare bright spikes.
option.GEOMETRY_BUDGET=Triangle Capacity
option.GEOMETRY_BUDGET.comment=Maximum captured triangles. Red diagnostics mean incomplete capture; missing occluders can leak light. Raise capacity or reduce range.
option.GEOMETRY_RAY_TESTS=Traversal Budget
option.GEOMETRY_RAY_TESTS.comment=Maximum BVH node visits per ray. Exhaustion blocks the ray conservatively. Raise if complex silhouettes turn dark.
option.CUTOUT_THRESHOLD=Texture alpha cutoff
option.CUTOUT_THRESHOLD.comment=Shadow and world rays pass through texture samples below this alpha value. Does not make opaque models transparent.
option.RAY_BIAS=Ray Origin Offset
option.RAY_BIAS.comment=Small offset from the actual geometric plane. Excessively high values can miss thin geometry.
option.POWDER_EMISSION=Concrete powder emission
option.POWDER_EMISSION.comment=Makes concrete powder an area emitter with its material color. Disabled by default in every profile.
value.POWDER_EMISSION.0=Off
value.POWDER_EMISSION.1=On
option.POWDER_STRENGTH=Concrete powder brightness
option.SUN_WARMTH=Sun warmth
option.MOON_INTENSITY=Moon intensity
option.CUSTOM_SKY=Atmosphere colors
option.CUSTOM_SKY.comment=Uses an analytic environment as the path-traced light source. Off uses the game sky color; this is not a spectral atmosphere simulation.
