option.PT_LIGHT_CANDIDATES=Emitter Candidates
option.PT_LIGHT_CANDIDATES.comment=Importance-resample several emitting triangles before one visibility ray. Reduces dark samples around small light sources; costs source sampling work.
option.PT_TRANSMISSION_DEPTH=Interface Limit
option.PT_TRANSMISSION_DEPTH.comment=Maximum water/glass interfaces, separate from diffuse and volume events. Low limits can cut off nested transparent paths.
option.SMALL_LIGHT_BOOST=Small Light Power
option.SMALL_LIGHT_BOOST.comment=Radiance multiplier for torches, lanterns, end rods and other mapped small emitters. Changes actual emitted energy in all light paths.

option.PT_TRANSMISSION_FILTER=Water and Glass Filter
option.PT_TRANSMISSION_FILTER.comment=Variance-guided noise filtering for glass, water and underwater scattering. Raise for smoother transmission; lower for sharper secondary detail. Opaque material textures remain full resolution.

# Water focusing and world-space participating clouds.
screen.CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.PT_CAUSTIC_SOLVER_STEPS=Caustic Guide Refinement
option.PT_CAUSTIC_SOLVER_STEPS.comment=Iterations for the refracted-sun proposal. Higher values improve deep-water focusing; actual paths, visibility and Fresnel still determine radiance.
option.PT_WATER_SAMPLES=Water Sample Multiplier
option.PT_WATER_SAMPLES.comment=Multiply camera paths only for water-covered pixels or an underwater camera. Reduces caustic noise at additional GPU cost. Requires Water and Caustics.
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.comment=World-space heterogeneous medium in the path integrator. Visible to primary, reflection and transmission rays. Requires Volumetric Scattering; Overworld only.
value.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.0=Off
value.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.1=On
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Light Attenuation
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Attenuate direct light connections through cloud density, including self-shadowing. Disable for an artistic, nonphysical result.
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.1=On
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Fraction of the procedural density field that forms clouds. Zero produces a clear sky.
option.CLOUD_DENSITY=Cloud Extinction
option.CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=Maximum extinction per block. Higher values produce thicker, darker cloud interiors; no emissive cloud fill is added.
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT=Cloud Base Height
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=Cloud-layer base in absolute world Y coordinates.
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Cloud Layer Thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Vertical size of the participating medium in blocks.
option.CLOUD_SCALE=Cloud Shape Scale
option.CLOUD_SCALE.comment=Horizontal size of the 3D density features in blocks.
option.CLOUD_WIND_SPEED=Cloud Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_WIND_SPEED.comment=World-space advection in blocks per second. Zero freezes the density field.
option.CLOUD_WIND_ANGLE=Cloud Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Horizontal wind direction in degrees: 0 is +X and 90 is +Z.
option.CLOUD_DISTANCE=Cloud Ray Distance
option.CLOUD_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum cloud transport distance in blocks. Independent of the captured terrain distance. Also applies to reflections.
option.CLOUD_STEPS=Cloud Density Steps
option.CLOUD_STEPS.comment=Bounded optical-depth integration steps per continuation segment. Higher values resolve distant/small features more accurately.
option.CLOUD_SHADOW_STEPS=Cloud Shadow Steps
option.CLOUD_SHADOW_STEPS.comment=Density integration steps per direct-light connection. Higher values reduce shadow integration error.
option.CLOUD_ANISOTROPY=Cloud Forward Scattering
option.CLOUD_ANISOTROPY.comment=Henyey-Greenstein phase asymmetry. Zero is isotropic; larger values concentrate scattering toward the sun direction.
option.CLOUD_ALBEDO=Cloud Scattering Albedo
option.CLOUD_ALBEDO.comment=Fraction of cloud extinction that scatters instead of absorbing. One is a conservative medium.
option.CLOUD_HISTORY=Cloud History Limit
option.CLOUD_HISTORY.comment=Maximum temporal samples for a primary ray crossing the cloud layer. Lower values reduce trails from moving clouds; higher values reduce noise.
option.CLOUD_FILTER=Cloud Reconstruction Strength
option.CLOUD_FILTER.comment=Variance-guided spatial reconstruction for primary rays crossing the cloud layer. Requires Spatial Reconstruction. Zero disables the cloud blend; increasing it smooths fine cloud detail.

